{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c355","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1833c-5db9-7c13-8ce4-12f397c1cfa6"},"sequence":5,"recorded_at":1780531400000005,"record_type":"status","durability":"ephemeral","causation_id":"01a1833c-5f91-7a83-9a6c-d885674ebe8f","payload_type":"turn.input.user","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"command_id":"01a1833c-5f91-7a83-9a6c-d885674ebe8f","kind":"turn_input_user","prompt":"Implement docs/tasks/41-read-aloud.md in this repo (LectorIA-meta). Read it fully, plus docs/contracts/narration.md, core/narration.ts, app/reader.tsx, app/player.tsx, app/icons.tsx, app/skin.ts, app/tokens.css, core/reader.ts and the Folio reader in app/folio and app/leer.\nRules: follow AGENTS.md and RESCUE_LOG.md. Keep files small (the pre-commit size hook rejects files over about 5k tokens, so split modules). No hex or rgb literals outside the tokens files, and no inline <svg> outside app/icons.tsx. No secrets. Never use --no-verify. Do not run `next start` or `next dev`.\nAdd a row for \"41: read aloud\" to BUILT_DURING_HACKATHON.md.\nWork in small commits (the prepare-commit-msg hook adds the co-author trailer). Run npm test, npm run typecheck, npm run check:size and npm run check:secrets before finishing. Note: locally pipeline/ingest.test.ts fails on Node 20 because of jsdom/undici; that is pre-existing and CI uses Node 22, so ignore it only.\nWhen done, print a short summary of the files changed and any open questions.","run_stream":{"id":"01a1833c-5f91-7a83-9a6c-d885674ebe8f","kind":"run"}}}
