{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c383","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1833c-5db9-7c13-8ce4-12f397c1cfa6"},"sequence":28,"recorded_at":1780531400000051,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a1833c-5f91-7a83-9a6c-d885674ebe8f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"command_id":"01a1833c-5f91-7a83-9a6c-d885674ebe8f","event":{"chunk":"Read text file `docs/tasks/41-read-aloud.md`.\n1|# 41 · Read aloud in the reader\n2|\n3|Builds on task 40 (core/narration.ts, docs/contracts/narration.md, data/books/oz/narration.json, public/narration/v2/...). App code only; no pipeline or Modal changes.\n4|\n5|## What the reader gets\n6|\n7|A \"Read aloud\" control that plays the per-chapter Kokoro narration and follows it in the text, word by word, like Kindle/Audible read-along.\n8|\n9|- **Control.** Its own component, `app/narration/read-aloud.tsx`, placed in the reader chrome (check app/folio for the current Folio layout; other agents are editing it, so keep the touch points small) (plus a controller hook in `app/narration/`). Play/pause, a narration volume slider, and an on/off state persisted in localStorage `lectoria.narration.v1` as `{on, volume}`. Light mode is the default. Icon: a new `\"read-aloud\"` entry in `app/icons.tsx` (an open book with two sound-wave arcs), never an emoji, never an inline `<svg>` elsewhere. Colours only from tokens (add tokens to app/tokens.css where needed; no hex or rgb literals in components; skin-ready tests must stay green).\n10|- **Copy.** Warm English. Button label \"Read aloud\" / \"Pause\". While a chapter is not ready yet: \"Getting the voice ready…\". Error: \"The voice isn't available right now.\" Never use the word \"Generated\".\n11|- **Where it lives.** The controller sits in the layout-level `app/reader.tsx` so it survives scene navigation. It loads each chapter's manifest lazily. data/books/oz/narration.json is about 1 MB with every manifest inline, so it must never reach the client: the server layout derives a small `{chapter → {src, manifest}}` map (the manifest URL is `src` with `.mp3` replaced by `.json`, already served from public/) and passes only that and uses one dedicated `<audio>` element. It is separate from `core/music-session.ts` except for one ducking signal.\n12|- **Continuity.** Playback seeks to the scene's span (`sceneSpan`) and continues into the next scene and the next chapter without user action.\n13|- **Auto page-turn.** When the active word leaves the current sub-page, turn the sub-page (or go to the next scene) automatically, unless the user navigated by hand in the last ~8 s; in that case keep reading and do not yank them back. Pause stays paused across turns.\n14|- **Ducking.** While the voice plays, the music ducks about −18 dB via a `duck` multiplier on the Player, ramped over ~400 ms down and ~800 ms back up. The rain layer is not ducked.\n15|\n16|## Word highlight\n17|\n18|- Sync in a requestAnimationFrame loop that reads `audio.currentTime` and uses `activeWordAt` / `activeChunkAt` from core/narration.ts. It must survive seek, pause and playbackRate changes (no timers that drift).\n19|- Map word timings to the DOM with fragment offsets: add a `from` character offset to the fragments `paginateScene` (core/reader.ts) produces, so cont fragments of a split paragraph know where they start. Build Ranges on the `<p data-n>` text nodes.\n20|- Current sentence: soft tint via the CSS Custom Highlight API (`CSS.highlights`, `::highlight(narration-sentence)`), with a no-op fallback where unsupported.\n21|- Current word: an absolutely positioned overlay mark placed from `range.getClientRects()` (do not change layout; pagination must not reflow).\n22|- Scroll the active word into view gently only if it is off screen; instant under `prefers-reduced-motion`, and no mark transitions then.\n23|- Click a word to seek there (`wordAt`), only while narration is on.\n24|\n25|### Highlight style per skin (Martin's decision)\n26|\n27|Martin picked the second treatment of each skin from /workspace/prototypes/highlight/. The style is chosen by `html[data-skin]`; any skin that is not one of the three below, including today's `\"default\"`, uses engraving.\n28|\n29|| skin id      | word mark | sentence tint |\n30||--------------|-----------|---------------|\n31|| `engraving` (default fallback) | small-caps emphasis on a 1px hairline rule under the word | very faint ink tint |\n32|| `watercolor` | warm sienna bleed swatch with a darker pooled edge, slightly irregular border-radius, tiny blur | faint cool wash |\n33|| `ink-doodle` | loose hand-drawn circle (SVG path from the icon registry style, stroke from tokens) around the word | faint ink tint |\n34|\n35|Implementation notes:\n36|- Put the treatment mapping in one small pure function, e.g. `highlightStyleFor(skin: string): \"engraving\" | \"watercolor\" | \"ink-doodle\"`, with a unit test (unknown → engraving).\n37|- Small caps must not reflow the page: render the active word in small caps inside the overlay (a clone of the word on a paper-coloured background sized to the word's rect) rather than restyling the text in flow.\n38|- Mark colours, rule weight and tints are tokens (e.g. `--narration-mark`, `--narration-mark-edge`, `--narration-sentence`) with light and dark values.\n39|- Reference CSS from the prototype (port values into tokens; do not copy hex literals into components):\n40|  - watercolor bleed: `background: rgba(214,134,96,.30); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1.5px rgba(184,98,62,.35), 0 0 6px rgba(214,134,96,.25); border-radius: 40% 60% 52% 48%/50% 46% 54% 50%; filter: blur(.4px)`; placed at word rect inset −3px horizontally.\n41|  - ink circle: path `M50 -2 C 80 -3, 104 10, 100 28 C 96 44, 20 46, 4 30 C -6 16, 18 1, 56 2` in viewBox `0 0 100 44`, preserveAspectRatio none, stroke-width 1.8, round caps; box = word rect expanded 6px x, 3px y. The SVG must come from `app/icons.tsx` (add an icon-like entry or a dedicated exported shape there).\n42|  - engraving: `font-variant: small-caps; letter-spacing: .04em; font-weight: 600`, rule 1px at word bottom −2px.\n43|  - mark movement: `transition: left/top/width/height 120ms ease-out`, none under reduced motion.\n44|\n45|## Done when\n46|\n47|- Unit tests for: highlightStyleFor, fragment `from` offsets, word→range mapping (punctuation, curly quotes, split paragraphs), auto-turn suppression after manual navigation, prefs persistence, duck ramp.\n48|- npm test, typecheck, check:size, check:secrets, skin-ready/icon tests green. Do not run `next start`.","final_result":true,"kind":"output","task_id":"01a1833c-68cc-7bc1-8a65-ea942a719cb8"},"kind":"task_lifecycle","run_stream":{"id":"01a1833c-5f91-7a83-9a6c-d885674ebe8f","kind":"run"},"task_id":"01a1833c-68cc-7bc1-8a65-ea942a719cb8","task_stream":{"id":"01a1833c-68cc-7bc1-8a65-ea942a719cb8","kind":"task"}}}
