{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3f1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1833c-5db9-7c13-8ce4-12f397c1cfa6"},"sequence":83,"recorded_at":1780531400000161,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a1833c-5f91-7a83-9a6c-d885674ebe8f","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"call_id":"call_01a1833c6b46713a85012a0ad6bb3213","command_id":"01a1833c-5f91-7a83-9a6c-d885674ebe8f","correlation_facts":{"outcome":"success","tool_name":"read_file"},"kind":"tool_result","run_stream":{"id":"01a1833c-5f91-7a83-9a6c-d885674ebe8f","kind":"run"},"text":"Read text file `docs/contracts/narration.md`.\n1|# Narration\n2|\n3|Read-aloud narration, one compact mp3 per chapter plus a per-chapter\n4|manifest with sentence timings. The unit is the chapter (owner\n5|decision): the reader plays any scene by seeking to its first sentence\n6|(`sceneSpan`) and highlights the sentence being read (`activeChunkAt`).\n7|Voice Kokoro-82M `af_heart` at speed 0.95, generated on a Modal GPU\n8|function that scales to zero.\n9|\n10|## Manifest\n11|\n12|`ChapterNarration` in `core/narration.ts`: `format: 2`, `key`, `src`,\n13|`durationSec`, `voice`, `model`, `speed`, and `chunks` with `n`\n14|(paragraph ordinal), `start`/`end` (char offsets into the paragraph),\n15|`t0`/`t1` (seconds), and `w` (word timings, below).\n16|`parseChapterNarration` throws on any bad field: it is a trust\n17|boundary, since the reader fetches this JSON. `src` is an `https:`\n18|URL or a same-origin path under `/narration/`.\n19|\n20|## Word timings\n21|\n22|No forced alignment: the Modal function returns each Kokoro token\n23|timestamp with chapter-absolute seconds per span, and `alignWords`\n24|maps them onto display words (`/[\\p{L}\\p{N}]+(?:['’][\\p{L}\\p{N}]+)*/u`,\n25|so \"Oz’s\" and \"didn't\" are one word and punctuation never\n26|highlights). Both sides compare on NFKD lowercase letters and digits\n27|with apostrophes dropped, in order with a lookahead of 3 either way;\n28|a token spanning several display words (\"well-known\") splits its time\n29|by character length. Words left without time interpolate between\n30|their neighbours; all times are clamped to the span and monotonic.\n31|`w` is flat `[start, end, t0, t1, ...]` with paragraph-relative char\n32|offsets and seconds, validated (multiple of 4, offsets in range,\n33|times in range, sorted) and required. `activeWordAt` drives the\n34|highlight, `wordAt` drives click-to-seek. Cost: 4 numbers per word,\n35|about 25 KB per chapter manifest.\n36|\n37|## Cache key\n38|\n39|`narrationKeyInput` builds a canonical string from the\n40|NFC-normalized, whitespace-collapsed chunk texts joined with `\"\\n\"`,\n41|plus voice, model, speed, and format. Callers hash it with SHA-256;\n42|`narrationKey` returns `narration/v2/<voice>/<first 32 hex>`. Same\n43|text + voice + model + speed gives the same key, any edit gives a new\n44|one. Audio lives at `<key>.mp3`, the manifest at `<key>.json`, as\n45|deterministic public Blob paths; the Redis index `narr:idx:<key>`\n46|holds the manifest JSON. Oz is pregenerated through the same keys, so\n47|a second reader of the same text gets it free.\n48|\n49|## Concurrency\n50|\n51|One reusable function, `ensureChapterNarration` in\n52|`core/narration-cache.ts`, serves the offline Oz run and the future\n53|upload route: index hit, then store hit with index backfill, then lock\n54|`narr:lock:<key>` (TTL 300 s, `setNxEx`; a null acquire means\n55|`pending`), one index re-check, budget reserve, synthesize, put audio\n56|and manifest, index set, release. Cache hits never touch the lock or\n57|the budget; failures refund once and release. No error text leaves the\n58|function.\n59|\n60|## Spend\n61|\n62|Integer micro-dollars. `estimateNarrationMicro(chars)` reserves the\n63|cap before generating: about 15 chars of audio per second, GPU time\n64|about 2% of audio after encode, plus 8 s of cold start/overhead, at\n65|the A10G rate (`KOKORO_GPU_USD_PER_SEC`, about USD 1.10/h). The Modal\n66|function tries GPUs in order `[\"L4\", \"A10G\", \"T4\"]`, and caps use the\n67|A10G rate so they stay conservative whichever GPU serves. The\n68|server reserves on both the global spend key and the daily spend key\n69|(`spendKey()`, `dailySpendKey(day)` from `core/images`), refunding\n70|both past either cap; the global `DAILY_SPEND_CAP_USD` applies. The\n71|offline run caps with `NARRATION_CAP_USD` (default 2) and stops with a\n72|report instead of spending more. Worked number: an average Oz chapter\n73|of ~9,000 chars is about 10 min of audio, about 20 s of warm GPU,\n74|about USD 0.006.\n75|\n76|## Rolling window\n77|\n78|The owner warms two chapters ahead: at upload, chapters 1 and 2 while\n79|the book is processed; entering chapter N ensures N+1 and N+2; jumping\n80|to N ensures N and N+1. `chaptersToPrepare` in `core/narration.ts`\n81|computes the window; the client asks, the server dedupes through the\n82|index and lock.\n83|\n84|## Cold start\n85|\n86|About 15–30 s for the first chapter after the function scaled to zero\n87|(`scaledown_window=60`), warm calls a few seconds per chapter. The\n88|2-ahead window hides it after chapter 1. While a chapter is pending,\n89|the Read aloud control shows a quiet \"Getting the voice ready…\"\n90|state.\n91|\n92|## Operations\n93|\n94|Deploy with `modal deploy pipeline/modal/narrate.py`; the app\n95|`lectoria-narration` scales to zero a minute after the last call, and\n96|`modal app stop lectoria-narration` removes it entirely.\n97|\n98|## Open items\n99|\n100|Upload route wiring (uses `server/narration/cache.ts`, no route yet);\n101|Blob vs `public/` for Oz (same keys either way, so switching is a\n102|re-run)."}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3f3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1833c-5db9-7c13-8ce4-12f397c1cfa6"},"sequence":84,"recorded_at":1780531400000163,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a1833c-5f91-7a83-9a6c-d885674ebe8f","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"call_id":"call_01a1833c6c8c741d8b85f9ef97013691","command_id":"01a1833c-5f91-7a83-9a6c-d885674ebe8f","correlation_facts":{"outcome":"success","tool_name":"read_file"},"kind":"tool_result","run_stream":{"id":"01a1833c-5f91-7a83-9a6c-d885674ebe8f","kind":"run"},"text":"Read text file `core/narration.ts`.\n1|// Pure narration logic: sentence split, chunking, cache keys, manifest\n2|// validation, playback helpers, and cost math. No env, no network,\n3|// no crypto, no node: imports; callers inject hashing.\n4|export const NARRATION_VOICE = \"af_heart\";\n5|export const NARRATION_MODEL = \"kokoro-82m/0.9.4\";\n6|export const NARRATION_SPEED = 0.95;\n7|export const NARRATION_FORMAT = 2;\n8|export const SENTENCE_GAP_SEC = 0.3;\n9|export const PARAGRAPH_GAP_SEC = 0.7;\n10|\n11|export interface SentenceSpan {\n12|  start: number;\n13|  end: number;\n14|}\n15|\n16|export interface NarrationChunk {\n17|  n: number;\n18|  start: number;\n19|  end: number;\n20|  text: string;\n21|}\n22|\n23|const CLOSERS = new Set([\"”\", \"’\", '\"', \"'\", \")\", \"]\"]);\n24|\n25|// Lowercase words that end with a period without ending a sentence.\n26|const ABBREVIATIONS = new Set([\n27|  \"mr\", \"mrs\", \"ms\", \"dr\", \"st\", \"mt\", \"prof\", \"sr\", \"jr\",\n28|  \"rev\", \"lt\", \"col\", \"gen\", \"capt\", \"sgt\", \"ave\", \"blvd\", \"rd\", \"no\",\n29|]);\n30|\n31|function isTerminator(char: string): boolean {\n32|  return char === \".\" || char === \"!\" || char === \"?\" || char === \"…\";\n33|}\n34|\n35|function isSpace(char: string | undefined): boolean {\n36|  return char === undefined || /\\s/.test(char);\n37|}\n38|\n39|// Word of letters directly before index (exclusive), lowercased.\n40|function wordBefore(text: string, index: number): string {\n41|  let i = index - 1;\n42|  while (i >= 0 && /[A-Za-z]/.test(text[i] as string)) i -= 1;\n43|  return text.slice(i + 1, index).toLowerCase();\n44|}\n45|\n46|function wordCount(piece: string): number {\n47|  const words = piece.split(/\\s+/).filter((w) => w.length > 0);\n48|  return words.length;\n49|}\n50|\n51|// Char offsets into the paragraph text, trimmed of surrounding\n52|// whitespace, covering every non-space char. A sentence ends at a\n53|// terminator plus closing quotes/brackets followed by whitespace.\n54|export function splitSentences(text: string): SentenceSpan[] {\n55|  const raw: SentenceSpan[] = [];\n56|  let pieceStart = -1;\n57|  let i = 0;\n58|  while (i < text.length) {\n59|    const char = text[i] as string;\n60|    if (/\\s/.test(char)) {\n61|      i += 1;\n62|      continue;\n63|    }\n64|    if (pieceStart === -1) pieceStart = i;\n65|    if (isTerminator(char)) {\n66|      let end = i + 1;\n67|      while (end < text.length && CLOSERS.has(text[end] as string)) end += 1;\n68|      if (isSpace(text[end])) {\n69|        if (char === \".\") {\n70|          const word = wordBefore(text, i);\n71|          const singleInitial = /^[A-Z]$/.test(text.slice(i - 1, i));\n72|          if (singleInitial || ABBREVIATIONS.has(word)) {\n73|            i += 1;\n74|            continue;\n75|          }\n76|        }\n77|        // Trim trailing whitespace inside the piece (there is none:\n78|        // the piece ends at a terminator or closer).\n79|        raw.push({ start: pieceStart, end });\n80|        pieceStart = -1;\n81|        i = end;\n82|        continue;\n83|      }\n84|    }\n85|    i += 1;\n86|  }\n87|  if (pieceStart !== -1) {\n88|    let end = text.length;\n89|    while (end > pieceStart && /\\s/.test(text[end - 1] as string)) end -= 1;\n90|    raw.push({ start: pieceStart, end });\n91|  }\n92|  if (raw.length === 0) return [];\n93|  // Merge a piece shorter than 3 words into the previous sentence\n94|  // (or the next one if first), keeping offsets exact.\n95|  const merged: SentenceSpan[] = [];\n96|  for (const span of raw) {\n97|    const piece = text.slice(span.start, span.end);\n98|    if (wordCount(piece) >= 3 || merged.length === 0) {\n99|      merged.push({ ...span });\n100|      continue;\n101|    }\n102|    const prev = merged[merged.length - 1] as SentenceSpan;\n103|    prev.end = span.end;\n104|  }\n105|  if (merged.length > 1) {\n106|    const first = merged[0] as SentenceSpan;\n107|    if (wordCount(text.slice(first.start, first.end)) < 3) {\n108|      const next = merged[1] as SentenceSpan;\n109|      next.start = first.start;\n110|      merged.shift();\n111|    }\n112|  }\n113|  return merged;\n114|}\n115|\n116|export function chapterChunks(paragraphs: { n: number; text: string }[]): {\n117|  chunks: NarrationChunk[];\n118|  gaps: number[];\n119|} {\n120|  const chunks: NarrationChunk[] = [];\n121|  const paraOf: number[] = [];\n122|  paragraphs.forEach((para, paraIndex) => {\n123|    for (const span of splitSentences(para.text)) {\n124|      chunks.push({ n: para.n, start: span.start, end: span.end, text: para.text.slice(span.start, span.end) });\n125|      paraOf.push(paraIndex);\n126|    }\n127|  });\n128|  const gaps = chunks.map((_, i) => {\n129|    if (i === chunks.length - 1) return 0;\n130|    return paraOf[i] !== paraOf[i + 1] ? PARAGRAPH_GAP_SEC : SENTENCE_GAP_SEC;\n131|  });\n132|  return { chunks, gaps };\n133|}\n134|\n135|export function normalizeChunkText(text: string): string {\n136|  return text.normalize(\"NFC\").replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").trim();\n137|}\n138|\n139|// Canonical string the caller hashes with SHA-256. Same text + voice +\n140|// model + speed => same string; any edit changes it.\n141|export function narrationKeyInput(args: {\n142|  chunks: { text: string }[];\n143|  voice: string;\n144|  model: string;\n145|  speed: number;\n146|  format: number;\n147|}): string {\n148|  const body = args.chunks.map((c) => normalizeChunkText(c.text)).join(\"\\n\");\n149|  return `narration/${args.format}\\nvoice:${args.voice}\\nmodel:${args.model}\\nspeed:${args.speed}\\n${body}`;\n150|}\n151|\n152|export function narrationKey(hashHex: string, voice: string): string {\n153|  return `narration/v${NARRATION_FORMAT}/${voice}/${hashHex.slice(0, 32)}`;\n154|}\n155|\n156|export function narrationAudioPath(key: string): string {\n157|  return `${key}.mp3`;\n158|}\n159|\n160|export function narrationManifestPath(key: string): string {\n161|  return `${key}.json`;\n162|}\n163|\n164|export interface ChapterChunkTiming {\n165|  n: number;\n166|  start: number;\n167|  end: number;\n168|  t0: number;\n169|  t1: number;\n170|  // Flat word timings: [start, end, t0, t1, ...] with start/end\n171|  // paragraph-relative char offsets inside start..end and times in\n172|  // seconds. Built by alignWords in ensureChapterNarration.\n173|  w: number[];\n174|}\n175|\n176|export interface ChapterNarration {\n177|  format: 2;\n178|  key: string;\n179|  src: string;\n180|  durationSec: number;\n181|  voice: string;\n182|  model: string;\n183|  speed: number;\n184|  chunks: ChapterChunkTiming[];\n185|}\n186|\n187|function isRecord(json: unknown): json is Record<string, unknown> {\n188|  return typeof json === \"object\" && json !== null && !Array.isArray(json);\n189|}\n190|\n191|// Strict parse at the trust boundary: the reader fetches this JSON,\n192|// so any bad field throws instead of half-playing.\n193|export function parseChapterNarration(json: unknown): ChapterNarration {\n194|  if (!isRecord(json)) throw new Error(\"invalid narration manifest\");\n195|  if (json.format !== NARRATION_FORMAT) throw new Error(\"invalid narration manifest\");\n196|  if (typeof json.key !== \"string\" || json.key.length === 0) throw new Error(\"invalid narration manifest\");\n197|  if (typeof json.src !== \"string\" || !isSafeSrc(json.src)) throw new Error(\"invalid n