{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dc93","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1833c-5db9-7c13-8ce4-12f397c1cfa6"},"sequence":3236,"recorded_at":1780531400006467,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a1833c-5f91-7a83-9a6c-d885674ebe8f","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"command_id":"01a1833c-5f91-7a83-9a6c-d885674ebe8f","kind":"run_terminal","reason":null,"run_stream":{"id":"01a1833c-5f91-7a83-9a6c-d885674ebe8f","kind":"run"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Done. Read-aloud is implemented across 6 small commits.\n\nFiles changed:\n- [core/reader.ts](/workspace/wt-41/core/reader.ts) + test: `from` offsets on all `paginateScene` fragments.\n- [app/icons.tsx](/workspace/wt-41/app/icons.tsx): `read-aloud` (book + two arcs) and `ink-circle` registry entries, no inline SVG elsewhere.\n- [app/tokens.css](/workspace/wt-41/app/tokens.css): `--narration-*` tokens with light/dark values and watercolor/ink-doodle overrides; components/CSS use only `var()`.\n- New [app/narration/](/workspace/wt-41/app/narration): `types`, `prefs` (localStorage `lectoria.narration.v1`), `highlight-style` (`highlightStyleFor`, unknown → engraving), `duck` (`rampDuck`, −18 dB over 400/800 ms), `turn` (`shouldAutoTurn`, 8 s window), `word-map` + `ranges` (fragment-relative word/sentence planning), `use-narration` (layout-level controller, one `<audio>`, lazy manifest fetch, span seek, scene/chapter advance), `context` (provider), `read-aloud` (control), `read-sync` (rAF follow loop, Highlight API sentence tint with no-op fallback, overlay mark, gentle off-screen scroll, reduced-motion handling, click-to-seek via `wordAt`).\n- [app/styles/narration.css](/workspace/wt-41/app/styles/narration.css) (imported from `globals.css`): control + per-treatment mark geometry.\n- [app/reader.tsx](/workspace/wt-41/app/reader.tsx): provider wraps the shell; `BandPlay` feeds `duck` to [app/player.tsx](/workspace/wt-41/app/player.tsx) (music only, rain untouched); [app/leer/layout.tsx](/workspace/wt-41/app/leer/layout.tsx) + new [server/narration.ts](/workspace/wt-41/server/narration.ts) pass only a small `{ch → src, manifest}` map (the 1 MB index stays server-side); [app/leer/scene-page.tsx](/workspace/wt-41/app/leer/scene-page.tsx) registers its scene, stamps manual moves, renders `data-from` and the mark.\n- [BUILT_DURING_HACKATHON.md](/workspace/wt-41/BUILT_DURING_HACKATHON.md): row 41.\n\nChecks: `npm test` 565 passed, 1 failed file — only `pipeline/ingest.test.ts`, the pre-existing Node 20 jsdom/undici breakage (this box is Node 20.19; all jsdom suites, including existing ones, fail the same way here; CI on Node 22 runs them). `typecheck`, `check:size`, `check:secrets` clean. New unit tests cover every item the brief lists: treatment mapping, `from` chaining, word→range planning with curly quotes/punctuation/split paragraphs, auto-turn suppression, prefs round-trip, duck curve. Never used `--no-verify`; never ran `next start/dev`.\n\nOpen questions / risks you should know:\n- I did not verify audio playback, the mark position, or the duck audibly — no browser run was possible here; worth one live pass (enable, seek, chapter cross, pause-across-turn, reduced motion).\n- Watercolor and ink-doodle treatments ship as CSS + tokens but can't be seen until those skins exist; at runtime everything renders engraving.\n- I skipped nothing from the brief."}}
